# Question 5: Music Playlist — Singly Linked List

**Problem Statement:**

A music application maintains songs in a playlist. Users can add songs to the playlist and remove a song when they no longer want it.

**Question:**

Implement a linked list playlist that supports:

1. Adding songs.
2. Removing a song.
3. Displaying the playlist.

**Sample Input:**

```text
4
ShapeOfYou
Believer
Perfect
Memories
Believer
```

**Sample Output:**

```text
Music Playlist:
ShapeOfYou
Believer
Perfect
Memories

After Removing Believer:
ShapeOfYou
Perfect
Memories
```

**Java Code:**

```java
import java.util.Scanner;

class Node {
    String song;
    Node next;

    Node(String song) {
        this.song = song;
        this.next = null;
    }
}

public class Main {
    Node head = null;

    // Add a song to the end of the playlist
    public void addSong(String song) {
        Node newNode = new Node(song);

        if (head == null) {
            head = newNode;
            return;
        }

        Node current = head;
        while (current.next != null) {
            current = current.next;
        }

        current.next = newNode;
    }

    // Remove the first matching song
    public void removeSong(String song) {
        if (head == null) {
            return;
        }

        if (head.song.equals(song)) {
            head = head.next;
            return;
        }

        Node current = head;
        while (current.next != null
                && !current.next.song.equals(song)) {
            current = current.next;
        }

        if (current.next != null) {
            current.next = current.next.next;
        }
    }

    // Display all songs
    public void displayPlaylist() {
        Node current = head;

        while (current != null) {
            System.out.println(current.song);
            current = current.next;
        }
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        Main playlist = new Main();

        int n = sc.nextInt();

        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            playlist.addSong(sc.next());
        }

        String remove = sc.next();

        System.out.println("Music Playlist:");
        playlist.displayPlaylist();

        playlist.removeSong(remove);

        System.out.println("\nAfter Removing " + remove + ":");
        playlist.displayPlaylist();

        sc.close();
    }
}
```

**Concept Used:**

* **Singly Linked List:** Each node stores a song and a reference to the next node.
* **Adding:** Inserts a song at the end of the playlist.
* **Removing:** Deletes the first matching song.
* **Displaying:** Traverses the list from the head to the last node.
